# walker simulate --lift --script test/sim/lift.walk
# SIMULATED lift board (src/sim/fakeLift.ts) and the real lift client, driven by a STAND-IN loop that plays the
# motion coordinator (not wired here): its keys stand for the screen's hold control and for Confirm presses.
# Real time: about 25 s.

expect lift link connected
expect lift state unhomed

# Home while holding the screen's lift control.
key lift-hold-on
expect lift hold on
key lift-home
expect lift accepted lift.home
expect 30000 lift ended lift.home completed

# Move up, and let go partway: it ramps down and stops, still homed.
key lift-up
expect lift accepted lift.move
wait 3000
key lift-hold-off
expect 2000 lift ended lift.move stopped

# Move again; the stop switch mid-move latches stop_circuit_opened.
key lift-hold-on
key lift-up
expect lift accepted lift.move
wait 1000
key lift-stop-switch
expect 2000 lift ended lift.move failed stop_circuit_opened
key lift-clear
expect 2000 lift clear refused cause_present
key lift-stop-switch
wait 500
key lift-clear
expect 2000 lift clear cleared

# The stop unhomed it: a move is refused until it homes again.
key lift-up
expect lift refused lift.move lift_not_homed
